1
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:36,490
Despite appearances, I think you'll find the city's on the rise.

2
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:41,180
Perhaps we should take shelter.

3
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,360
The city's on the rise?

4
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,750
Meereen is strong.

5
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:48,400
Commerce has returned to the markets.

6
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,770
The people are behind you.

7
00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:54,880
Well, not all the people, of course.

8
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:57,960
No ruler that ever lived had the support of all the people.

9
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:01,360
But the rebirth of Meereen is the cause of this violence.

10
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,570
The Masters cannot let Meereen succeed.

11
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:10,130
Because if Meereen succeeds, a city without slavery,

12
00:03:10,390 --> 00:03:11,940
a city without Masters...

13
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:15,990
it proves that no one needs a Master.

14
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,140
Good.

15
00:03:21,470 --> 00:03:22,590
Shall we begin?

16
00:03:24,590 --> 00:03:25,860
Do we have a plan?

17
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:27,980
I will crucify the Masters.

18
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:30,090
I will set their fleets afire,

19
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,030
kill every last one of their soldiers,

20
00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:33,870
and return their cities to the dirt.

21
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,540
That is my plan.

22
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:40,480
You don't approve?

23
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:43,060
You once told me you knew what your father was.

24
00:03:44,010 --> 00:03:45,900
Did you know his plans for King's Landing

25
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,060
when the Lannister armies were at his gates?

26
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:52,310
Probably not.

27
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,880
Well, he told my brother and Jaime told me.

28
00:03:56,430 --> 00:03:59,810
He had caches of wildfire hidden under the Red Keep,

29
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:02,290
the Guildhalls, the Sept of Baelor,

30
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:04,030
all the major thoroughfares.

31
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,230
He would have burned every one of his citizens.

32
00:04:08,890 --> 00:04:10,820
The loyal ones and the traitors.

33
00:04:11,270 --> 00:04:13,340
Every man, woman, and child.

34
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:14,840
That's why Jaime killed him.

35
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,250
This is entirely different.

36
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:18,440
You're talking about destroying cities.

37
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:20,620
It's not entirely different.

38
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:27,470
I'd like to suggest an alternate approach.

39
00:04:41,710 --> 00:04:43,900
Once before, I offered you peace.

40
00:04:44,770 --> 00:04:46,930
If you had not been so arrogant,

41
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:50,300
you could have returned to your homeland with a fleet of ships.

42
00:04:52,510 --> 00:04:55,890
Instead, you will flee Slaver's Bay on foot

43
00:04:57,320 --> 00:04:59,140
like the beggar queen you are.

44
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:02,150
We are here to discuss terms of surrender,

45
00:05:02,330 --> 00:05:04,220
not to trade insults.

46
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:06,460
The terms are simple.

47
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,690
You and your foreign friends will

48
00:05:08,690 --> 00:05:11,360
abandon the Great Pyramid and the city of Meereen.

49
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:14,240
The Unsullied you stole from Kraznys mo Nakloz

50
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:16,870
will remain to be sold again to the highest bidder.

51
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:20,270
The translator you stole from Kraznys mo Nakloz will remain

52
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:22,770
to be sold again to the highest bidder.

53
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:26,510
The dragons beneath the Great Pyramid will be slaughtered.

54
00:05:28,170 --> 00:05:30,180
We obviously didn't communicate clearly.

55
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,390
We're here to discuss your surrender, not mine.

56
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,070
I imagine it's difficult

57
00:05:39,820 --> 00:05:42,060
adjusting to the new reality.

58
00:05:44,710 --> 00:05:47,520
Your reign is over.

59
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:52,040
My reign has just begun.

60
00:08:31,330 --> 00:08:32,540
Dracarys.

61
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:38,120
Thank you for the armada.

62
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:40,060
Our queen does love ships.

63
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:44,560
Now, last time we spoke, we made a pact.

64
00:09:45,550 --> 00:09:47,270
You violated that pact.

65
00:09:47,580 --> 00:09:49,110
You declared war upon us.

66
00:09:49,230 --> 00:09:51,590
Though our queen does have a forgiving nature,

67
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:54,950
this cannot be forgiven.

68
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:57,930
Our queen insists that one of you must die

69
00:09:58,190 --> 00:10:00,260
as punishment for your crimes.

70
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:04,310
It always seems a bit abstract, doesn't it,

71
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:06,710
other people dying?

72
00:10:08,910 --> 00:10:10,630
Him. He should die.

73
00:10:10,630 --> 00:10:13,140
- Yes, him. - He's not one of us.

74
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:14,690
He's an outsider, a lowborn.

75
00:10:14,690 --> 00:10:16,260
He does not speak for us.

76
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:21,350
Please.

77
00:10:23,670 --> 00:10:24,700
Please.

78
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:45,680
Tell your people what happened here.

79
00:10:47,690 --> 00:10:50,300
Tell them you live by the grace of Her Majesty.

80
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,330
When they come forward with notions of retribution

81
00:10:53,330 --> 00:10:56,720
or ideas about returning the slave cities to their former glory,

82
00:10:58,080 --> 00:10:59,850
remind them what happened

83
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:03,340
when Daenerys Stormborn and her dragons came to Meereen.

84
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,140
You don't have to be here.

85
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,280
Yes, I do.

86
00:12:08,760 --> 00:12:10,010
My beloved wife.

87
00:12:12,860 --> 00:12:14,530
I've missed you terribly.

88
00:12:18,390 --> 00:12:21,130
Thank you for returning Lady Bolton safely.

89
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:24,160
Now, dismount and kneel before me,

90
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,620
surrender your army

91
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:28,790
and proclaim me the true Lord of Winterfell and Warden of the North.

92
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:31,400
I will pardon you for deserting the Night's Watch.

93
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:35,250
I will pardon these treasonous lords for betraying my house.

94
00:12:38,710 --> 00:12:40,450
Come, bastard,

95
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:44,150
you don't have the men, you don't have the horses,

96
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:45,960
and you don't have Winterfell.

97
00:12:46,710 --> 00:12:49,880
Why lead those poor souls into slaughter?

98
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,740
There's no need for a battle.

99
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:55,740
Get off your horse and kneel.

100
00:12:57,650 --> 00:12:59,150
I'm a man of mercy.

101
00:13:04,770 --> 00:13:05,780
You're right.

102
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,320
There's no need for a battle.

103
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:12,280
Thousands of men don't need to die.

104
00:13:14,770 --> 00:13:15,970
Only one of us.

105
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:20,220
Let's end this the old way.

106
00:13:20,630 --> 00:13:22,580
You against me.

107
00:13:35,150 --> 00:13:38,500
I keep hearing stories about you, bastard.

108
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,280
The way people in the North talk about you,

109
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:42,460
you're the greatest swordsman who ever walked.

110
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,200
Maybe you are that good.

111
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:47,980
Maybe not.

112
00:13:49,010 --> 00:13:50,700
I don't know if I'd beat you.

113
00:13:51,190 --> 00:13:54,000
But I know that my army will beat yours.

114
00:13:55,330 --> 00:13:56,300
I have 6,000 men.

115
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:59,860
You have, what, half that?

116
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:01,420
Not even?

117
00:14:01,420 --> 00:14:03,080
Aye, you have the numbers.

118
00:14:05,160 --> 00:14:06,650
Will your men want to fight for you

119
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:08,350
when they hear you wouldn't fight for them?

120
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:20,320
He's good. Very good.

121
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,220
Tell me, will you let your little brother die

122
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:26,400
because you're too proud to surrender?

123
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:28,120
How do we know you have him?

124
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:55,800
Now, if you want to save...

125
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:57,950
You're going to die tomorrow, Lord Bolton.

126
00:15:02,190 --> 00:15:03,320
Sleep well.

127
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:14,000
She's a fine woman, your sister.

128
00:15:15,330 --> 00:15:17,460
I look forward to having her back in my bed.

129
00:15:21,460 --> 00:15:23,150
And you're all fine-looking men.

130
00:15:23,950 --> 00:15:26,190
My dogs are desperate to meet you.

131
00:15:26,260 --> 00:15:28,800
I haven't fed them for seven days. They're ravenous.

132
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:32,250
I wonder which parts they'll try first.

133
00:15:32,730 --> 00:15:33,880
Your eyes?

134
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:36,010
Your balls?

135
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:39,700
We'll find out soon enough.

136
00:15:41,990 --> 00:15:45,340
In the morning, then, bastard.

137
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,650
If he was smart,

138
00:16:03,650 --> 00:16:06,330
he'd stay inside the walls of Winterfell and wait us out.

139
00:16:06,330 --> 00:16:09,370
That's not his way. He knows the North is watching.

140
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:12,420
If the other houses sense weakness on his part,

141
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,950
they'll stop fearing him.

142
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:17,030
He can't have that. Fear is his power.

143
00:16:17,030 --> 00:16:19,870
It's his weakness, too. His men don't want to fight for him.

144
00:16:19,870 --> 00:16:22,430
They're forced to fight for him. If they feel the tide turning...

145
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,390
It's not his men that worry me.

146
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,780
It's his horses.

147
00:16:26,130 --> 00:16:28,640
I know what mounted knights can do to us.

148
00:16:28,730 --> 00:16:31,580
You and Stannis cut through us like piss through snow.

149
00:16:32,050 --> 00:16:34,040
We're digging trenches all along our flanks.

150
00:16:34,050 --> 00:16:36,380
They won't be able to hit us the way that Stannis hit you,

151
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:37,640
in a double envelopment.

152
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,180
A pincer move.

153
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:51,080
They won't be able to hit us from the sides.

154
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:52,430
Good.

155
00:16:55,590 --> 00:16:58,210
It's crucial that we let them charge at us.

156
00:16:59,470 --> 00:17:01,830
They've got the numbers, we need the patience.

157
00:17:05,050 --> 00:17:07,730
If we let him buckle our center, he'll pursue.

158
00:17:08,990 --> 00:17:10,860
Then we'll have him surrounded on three sides.

159
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,430
Did you really think that cunt would fight you man-to-man?

160
00:17:16,610 --> 00:17:17,580
No.

161
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:20,040
But I wanted to make him angry.

162
00:17:23,070 --> 00:17:25,170
I want him coming at us full tilt.

163
00:17:27,160 --> 00:17:28,570
We should all get some sleep.

164
00:17:29,530 --> 00:17:32,740
Rest, Jon Snow. We need you sharp tomorrow.

165
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:45,000
So you've met the enemy,

166
00:17:45,690 --> 00:17:47,590
drawn up your battle plans.

167
00:17:48,930 --> 00:17:51,740
Aye, for what they're worth.

168
00:17:52,430 --> 00:17:56,030
You've known him for the space of a single conversation,

169
00:17:56,380 --> 00:17:57,840
you and your trusted advisors,

170
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:59,690
and you sit around making your plans

171
00:17:59,690 --> 00:18:02,580
on how to defeat a man you don't know.

172
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:04,320
I lived with him.

173
00:18:04,450 --> 00:18:06,090
I know the way his mind works.

174
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:08,500
I know how he likes to hurt people.

175
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:13,720
Did it ever once occur to you that I might have some insight?

176
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:16,930
You're right.

177
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:20,520
You think he's going to fall into your trap.

178
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:22,870
He won't. He's the one who lays traps.

179
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:25,960
- He's overconfident. - He plays with people.

180
00:18:26,130 --> 00:18:27,630
He's far better at it than you.

181
00:18:27,630 --> 00:18:28,630
He's been doing it all his life.

182
00:18:28,630 --> 00:18:30,220
Aye, and what have I been doing all my life?

183
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:31,650
Playing with broomsticks?

184
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:35,370
I fought beyond the Wall against worse than Ramsay Bolton.

185
00:18:35,370 --> 00:18:38,060
I've defended the Wall from worse than Ramsay Bolton.

186
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,220
You don't know him.

187
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,270
All right, tell me.

188
00:18:44,380 --> 00:18:47,250
What should we do? How do we get Rickon back?

189
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:50,760
We'll never get him back.

190
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:55,140
Rickon is Ned Stark's trueborn son,

191
00:18:55,140 --> 00:18:56,830
which makes him a greater threat to Ramsay

192
00:18:56,830 --> 00:18:59,160
than you, a bastard, or me, a girl.

193
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:01,110
As long as he lives,

194
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:03,100
Ramsay's claim to Winterfell will be contested,

195
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:07,120
which means he won't live long.

196
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:09,140
We can't give up on our brother.

197
00:19:09,150 --> 00:19:12,460
Listen to me, please. He wants you to make a mistake.

198
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:15,640
Of course he does. What should I do differently?

199
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:17,670
I don't know! I don't know anything about battles.

200
00:19:17,670 --> 00:19:21,510
Just don't do what he wants you to do.

201
00:19:21,510 --> 00:19:22,830
Aye, that's good advice.

202
00:19:22,880 --> 00:19:24,150
You think that's obvious?

203
00:19:24,150 --> 00:19:25,360
Well, it is a bit obvious.

204
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:26,780
If you had asked for my advice earlier,

205
00:19:26,780 --> 00:19:28,560
I would have told you not to attack Winterfell

206
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:31,010
until we had a larger force, or is that obvious, too?

207
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:33,340
When will we have a larger force?!

208
00:19:33,530 --> 00:19:35,510
We've pleaded with every house that'll have us.

209
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:37,140
The Blackfish can't help us.

210
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,780
We're lucky to have this many men.

211
00:19:38,780 --> 00:19:42,440
- It's not enough! - No, it's not enough. It's what we have!

212
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:50,730
Battles have been won against greater odds.

213
00:19:57,430 --> 00:19:58,810
If Ramsay wins,

214
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:00,890
I'm not going back there alive.

215
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:02,560
Do you understand me?

216
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:09,750
I won't let ever let him touch you again.

217
00:20:12,430 --> 00:20:14,380
I'll protect you, I promise.

218
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:17,750
No one can protect me.

219
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:20,270
No one can protect anyone.

220
00:20:39,050 --> 00:20:40,680
You think there's hope?

221
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:43,540
I've never seen these Bolton fuckers fight.

222
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,960
And they've never seen the free folk fight,

223
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:48,230
so, yes, there's hope.

224
00:20:50,050 --> 00:20:53,460
You want to avenge your king, don't you?

225
00:20:53,970 --> 00:20:56,440
It wasn't the Boltons defeated Stannis.

226
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:58,190
It was Stannis himself.

227
00:20:59,390 --> 00:21:00,790
I loved the man.

228
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:02,990
He lifted me up and made me something.

229
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:06,580
But he had demons in his skull whispering foul things.

230
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,770
- You saw these demons? - What?

231
00:21:10,530 --> 00:21:12,360
No, it's a manner of speaking.

232
00:21:14,390 --> 00:21:17,300
Not... actual demons.

233
00:21:19,970 --> 00:21:22,240
Well, you loved that cunt Stannis

234
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,320
and I loved the man he burned.

235
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,670
Mance didn't have demons in his skull.

236
00:21:26,670 --> 00:21:30,310
He didn't torch people or listen to some red witch.

237
00:21:31,090 --> 00:21:32,530
I believed in him.

238
00:21:32,910 --> 00:21:36,080
I thought he was the man to lead us through the Long Night.

239
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,830
But I was wrong just like you.

240
00:21:41,130 --> 00:21:44,190
Maybe that was our mistake, believing in kings.

241
00:21:45,990 --> 00:21:48,000
Jon Snow's not a king.

242
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,510
No, he's not.

243
00:21:54,850 --> 00:21:58,330
I need a good drink to help me sleep the night before a fight.

244
00:21:58,810 --> 00:22:00,030
You want some?

245
00:22:00,440 --> 00:22:02,700
I have a jug of sour goat's milk

246
00:22:02,700 --> 00:22:04,980
stronger than any of that grape water

247
00:22:04,990 --> 00:22:07,260
you southern twats like sucking on.

248
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:09,200
No, thanks. It does sound delicious,

249
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:11,210
but I better keep a clear head.

250
00:22:12,110 --> 00:22:14,300
I can never sleep the night before a battle.

251
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,500
So what do you do all night?

252
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:17,700
I walk.

253
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:19,800
Think and walk.

254
00:22:20,390 --> 00:22:22,610
Think and walk until I'm far enough away from camp

255
00:22:22,610 --> 00:22:24,980
that no one can hear me shitting my guts out.

256
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:28,120
Happy shitting.

257
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:43,500
My lady.

258
00:22:47,810 --> 00:22:49,730
You weren't at the war council.

259
00:22:51,570 --> 00:22:53,190
I'm not a soldier.

260
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:55,800
Any advice?

261
00:22:57,370 --> 00:22:58,770
Don't lose.

262
00:23:04,970 --> 00:23:07,140
If I do, if I fall...

263
00:23:09,590 --> 00:23:11,210
don't bring me back.

264
00:23:13,030 --> 00:23:14,450
I'll have to try.

265
00:23:14,450 --> 00:23:16,430
I'm ordering you not to bring me back.

266
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:18,040
I am not your servant, Jon Snow.

267
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:20,230
You're in my camp. I'm the commander.

268
